          </task>
        </exercise><exercise>
          <introduction>
            <p>
		In manufacturing processes the profit is usually a function of the number of units being produced, among other things. Suppose we are studying some small industrial company that produces <m>n</m> units in a week and makes a corresponding weekly profit of <m>P</m>. Assume <m>P =
	P(n)</m>.
	</p>
          </introduction><task>
            <p>
			If <m>P(1000)</m> = $500 and <m>P'(1000)</m> = $2/unit, then <md>P(1002) \approx \rule[-3pt]{0.5in}{0.3pt} \quad 
		    P(995) \approx \rule[-3pt]{0.5in}{0.3pt}\quad
